# Wisdom Page Skill

**This package: {{SKILL_SCOPE}}**

## 1. Trigger scope and exclusions

Use for: design analysis, component selection, Page Spec authoring and structural validation, cross-platform handoff, spec-only platform statements.
Do not use for: generating SwiftUI / Compose code directly, claiming a platform is compiled or verified, rendering UI in the App runtime, modifying platform APIs / ABI or consumer project configuration.

## 2. Three-mode routing

| Mode | Flow | Loaded content |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Design | request to Page Brief to Page Spec to structural validation to preview (optional) to design review | SKILL.md + page-spec + catalog short lines + tokens; never platform API |
| Single Platform | request to page pattern to target Provider to exact API to native template to business differences to platform verification | switch to the matching platform Provider package; Core provides semantics only |
| Cross Platform | one Page Spec to iOS Provider / Android Provider mapped separately, each verified separately | Core semantics + both Providers; never mechanically translate one platform into another |

The Core package has no Provider, API card, or native template. Any code-generation request must first identify the target platform and switch to the corresponding Provider; if absent, stop per section 8.

## 3. Entry points and forbidden reads

The only resident entry point is this file. `package:` paths resolve inside the package; `source-repo:` paths exist only in the wisdomdesign checkout.

Load on demand (`package:`): page-spec/{schema,extensions}.json, page-spec/examples/, catalog/{catalog.md,contracts-digest.json,components/WD*.md}, tokens/wisdom.tokens.json, runtime/{validate-spec,get-component,resolve-token,render-spec}.js.

Forbidden as normative sources: design/gallery/**, docs/02-components.md, review or audit narratives, platform internal symbols, uncompiled signature guesses.

Source priority, conflict order and the `source-repo:` list live in `package: REFERENCES.md` — load it before citing a spec line. Never retype a visual number: resolve it with runtime/resolve-token.js. Extension registry: `page-spec/extensions.json` is build output — never edit it in place; register in the source repo (see REFERENCES.md).

## 4. Page Brief and Page Spec

Write a Page Brief first: user intent, navigation skeleton, content pattern, primary action, states, accessibility title, acceptance items. Then write the Page Spec; structural validation proves structure only, not compilation or visual quality.

## 5. On-demand loading rules

- Selection: read catalog/catalog.md first; open one catalog/components/<ID>.md only after candidates narrow.
- Queries use runtime/get-component.js (<= 8 by default, cap 20); exact IDs return one card, never the library.
- Validation uses runtime/validate-spec.js; fix by code/jsonPath/message/suggestion, never bypass rules. Warnings are advisory, errors are blocking.
- Visual numbers: runtime/resolve-token.js --path <token>. Never retype a value from a card or the gallery.
- Platform APIs only inside the platform Provider package; Core carries no resident API data.

## 6. Scaffold and business modification boundary

Platform packages ship a scaffolder: `platforms/<id>/tools/scaffold.js --list`, then `--page <id> --workspace <dir> --as <FileName>.swift`. Run it before editing so the model never retypes the skeleton (it refuses overwrite and path escape). The model changes only business data, state, copy, actions and composition; never auto-modify dependencies, signing, navigation, build scripts or library source.

## 7. Verification loop

Structure: Page Spec validation + component existence + catalog anti-drift. Preview: runtime/render-spec.js shows layout from spec + tokens — layout evidence only, never visual sign-off. Native: compile / snapshot / UI / device run through platform repo commands, results in reports. Design: information architecture, primary-action hierarchy, state completeness confirmed by an independent design review. Passing one layer never substitutes the next; unexecuted layers are marked not-verified / not-evaluated. When structure passes: preview (runtime/render-spec.js) for layout review, resolve-token for exact values, or the platform Provider for code.

## 8. Stop conditions

Stop immediately and explain when any of these occurs; do not fabricate or paper over with extra prompts:
1. Unknown component, unknown parameter, unsourced API or signature.
2. Requirement missing intent / navigation / content pattern / primary action / states.
3. Target platform has no Provider, or capability is spec-only / unsupported / incompatible / not-verified.
4. Token / Contract / Provider / template versions incompatible, or dirty workspace while a release is requested.
5. Validation errors exceed the limited repair rounds, or path / overwrite / safety boundary is uncertain.

